1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,500
Millions of Indian shops track credit in a paper khata.

2
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:15,000
Khata stitches that notebook to voice, photos and chat, and its ghosts collect the dues.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Everyone who owes money becomes a ghost.

4
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:35,000
The most overdue haunts first.

5
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:45,000
"Ramesh ko 500 udhaar" means "500 on credit to Ramesh". Type the way you talk.

6
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Nothing is saved until you confirm.

7
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:05,000
"ਸੀਤਾ ਨੂੰ 300 ਉਧਾਰ": 300 on credit to Sita, in Punjabi script.

8
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Same customer: Ramesh, रमेश and ਰਮੇਸ਼ are one person.

9
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:27,000
On WhatsApp, just speak. A free Whisper model hears it.

10
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:40,000
The confirm button still guards the ledger.

11
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:50,000
Photograph a bill. It reads the total, then always asks who and which way.

12
00:01:50,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Text on the bill is never trusted as instructions.

13
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:08,000
Every entry is mirrored to Google Sheets.

14
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:15,000
Undo marks it cancelled. History is never deleted.

15
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:30,000
The séance drafts reminders in the customer's language. You decide whether to send.

16
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:40,000
The Lab shows every stitched part. Built with Kiro specs, steering and hooks, on free services only.
